Edit a repository's agent instructions and setup script on Settings → Repository variables.

A repository's own agent instructions, which the runner appends to its own,
and its setup script, which runs in the checkout before the agent starts, are
stored with its variables (omnigent_repo_env). The editor has a switch and a
text field for each, under the Git token and the variables; unlike values, the
text comes back to be edited, and switching a stored one off removes it on
save. The card lists them in its summary and shows their first lines. The
new-session badge adds an icon for each, and its popover says what they do.
"Add variable" and "Paste .env" move under the variables, and Cancel and Save
to the bottom of the editor. On a phone the fields take the full width, and
the script scrolls sideways instead of wrapping.
Both fields are highlighted with Shiki, which the chat's code blocks already
load lazily (HighlightedTextarea): the instructions as Markdown, the script as
shell or as the language its #! line names. The field stays a native
textarea with transparent text over a highlighted copy, so typing, selection
and phone keyboards work as before.
Base: omnigent v0.18.0 (a8676d23e88d), after 0001-0014.

